This repository is public solely so that its code and working process can be
read and evaluated. It is NOT open-source software.

1. Permitted
   a) Viewing and reading the repository's contents on GitHub.
   b) Cloning or downloading it for private, temporary evaluation — e.g. a
      hiring process, a work proposal or a technical review — without
      publishing it or running it in production.
   c) Quoting short excerpts with attribution in commentary, reviews or
      analysis, as permitted by applicable law.
   d) Whatever GitHub's Terms of Service grant its users over public
      repositories (viewing and forking within GitHub). That grant does not
      extend any permission in this license.

2. NOT permitted without the owner's prior written authorization
   a) Copying, reproducing, modifying, adapting, translating or creating
      derivative works of the code, design, 3D scene, shaders or
      architecture, in whole or in part.
   b) Publishing, distributing, sublicensing, selling, renting or deploying
      this project or any derivative version, commercially or otherwise.
   c) Using the content — texts, photographs, designs, audio, résumé, personal
      data, the names "Jonás Orbit" and "Jonás Javier", visual identity — for
      any purpose, or presenting this work or any part of it as your own.
   d) Using the repository or its contents to train, fine-tune or evaluate
      artificial intelligence models, or to build datasets.

3. Third parties
   Dependencies and third-party assets keep their own licenses, which prevail
   over this one where they apply.

4. No warranty
   The contents are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The owner
